<title>USA: Central estimates windfall tax at $180 mln.</title>
<headline>Central estimates windfall tax at $180 mln.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central and South West Corp said Thursday it estimates that a proposed one-time windfall tax liability on its SEEBOARD Plc unit would be about $180 million, depending on exchange rates.</p>
<p>The company made the announcement in light of a proposed windfall tax on the excess profits of privatized utilities in Britain. It said the $180 million estimate amounts to about 110 million British pounds.</p>
<p>CSW said payment of the tax is expected to be made in two equal installments, the first due December 1, 1997 and the second due by December 1, 1998.</p>
<p>CSW completed the acquisition of SEEBOARD in April 1996 at a cost of about $2.12 billion.</p>
